Module 2: Text Architecture & Typography (Heading, Paragraph, and Semantic Text)

Browser text ko kaise read karta hain, ab hum wo seekhenge.

1.Heading(<h1> to <h6>).
HTML mein 6 type ki headings hoti hain.

::: <h1> sabse badi aur sabse important hoti hain. Pure HTML page par sirf ek hi <h1> tag hona chahiye. Google search engine sabse phele apke <h1> ko hi padhta hai ki page kis baare mein hain.

::: <h6> sabse choti aur sabse kam important hoti hain.

Galti mat karna :: Log aksar text ko bada dikhane  ke liye <h1> use kar lete hain. yeh galat hai! text bada dikhane ke liye CSS use hoti hai. HTML tags sirf importance batane ke liye hote hain.


2.Structural Tags.

::: <p>(Paragraph): Text ko block mein break karta hai aur automatic upar-niche thodi khali jagah(margin) chod deta hain.

:::<br>(Line Break): Ye ek Empty tag ya Self-Closing tag hai (isko koi closing companion <br> nahi hota) . Ye chalte huye text ko wahi rok kar naye line par bhej deta hai.

:::<hr>(Horizontal Rule): Yeh bhi self-closing tag hai. yeh page par ek horizontal line khinch deta hai jb aapko koi topic change karna ho.


3.Semantic Emphasis(Style vs Meaning)
aksar log sochte hain ki <b> aur <strong> dono ka kaam text ko bold karna hai. Lekin coding ki duniya mein inka matlab alag hai:

:::<b> (Bold): Yeh sirf text ko mota (visual style) kar deta hain.Browser ke Liye iska koi special matlab nahi hai.

:::<strong> : Yeh text ko bold bhi karta hai aur browser  + Google ko batata hai ki Yeh text bahut zarooi(important) Hai. Screen readers is text to thoda zor se padhte hain.

:::<i> vs <em> (Emphasis): Same logic yahan bhi hai. <i> sirf text ko tedhs (italic) karta hai style ke liye, jabki <em> batata hai ki is shabd par stress/zor dena hai.


Example code jise aap dhyan se dekhiye:
<p>Humaara mission hai <strong>HTML5 mein expert</strong> banna.</p>
<p>Is kitab ke lekhak ka naam <i>Rahul Sharma</i> hai.</p>




